  "user_request_original": "Design and optimize a 20-layer alternating HfO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica substrate with air superstrate. Initialize thicknesses at [65, 114, 77, 93, 69, 108, 70, 96, 66, 67, 42, 83, 51, 89, 60, 67, 46, 70, 50, 70] nm (iteration_15 best candidate). Apply optimization bounds of ±15 nm (50% reduction from iteration_15's ±30 nm). Implement cooldown schedule: after 2 optimization iterations, lock layers 1-2 and 19-20 (outermost 4 layers) at their current values. Optimize remaining 16 layers using gradient_thickness optimizer. Evaluate at normal incidence, unpolarized light, coherent assumption across all layers. Spectrum: 400-1600 nm with 2001 points. Objectives: maximize mean transmittance in 1530-1565 nm, maximize mean reflectance in 400-700 nm. Robustness: relative uniform thickness uncertainty ±20% across 400-1600 nm. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1530-1565 nm, 400-700 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 1530-1565 nm band; High reflectance in 400-700 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: Low reflectance in 1530-1565 nm band; Low transmittance in 400-700 nm band. manufacturing constraints: Total layer count <= 30.",
